Hadith editions: app/src/main/assets/hadith/ and release translation packages
  Fawaz Ahmed's Hadith API, also the upstream source declared by UmmahAPI.
  Source revision: df57907be35291c91ad6a6691180e22ca9920784
  Retrieved November 15, 2026.
  https://github.com/fawazahmed0/hadith-api/tree/df57907be35291c91ad6a6691180e22ca9920784
  https://ummahapi.com/api/hadith/collections
  The upstream repository declares The Unlicense; its original text is preserved
  in licenses/Hadith-API-Unlicense.txt. This is not an independent clearance of
  underlying translation/publisher rights. The user requested offline use of
  this source after the uncertainty was disclosed. No new rights are asserted.
  Text is preserved verbatim as Unicode; conversion changes only packaging.
  Source author metadata is not treated as proof of translation authorship.
  Included: ara/eng-nawawi (42), ara/eng-qudsi (40), ara/eng-dehlawi (40).
  Optional: fra/tur/ben-nawawi, fra-qudsi, fra-dehlawi.
  Edition IDs, counts, SHA-256 hashes, numbering and structural audit limits
  are recorded in the catalogue and docs/hadith-source-audit.json.
  No scholarly verification or independent translator attribution is claimed.

Additional downloadable Hadith editions (v1.8.0)
  HadithAPI.com, authenticated source snapshot retrieved November 17, 2026.
  https://hadithapi.com/ and https://hadithapi.com/docs/hadiths
  Bukhari (7276), Muslim (7564), Tirmidhi (3956), Abu Dawud (5274),
  Ibn Majah (4341), Nasa'i (5761), and Mishkat (6293) Arabic source records.
  The provider states that its API service is free for everyone. No explicit
  public bulk/offline redistribution licence or request-rate limit was found.
  The app owner authorized offline use after reviewing that public statement.
  This is not independent clearance of translation/publisher rights, nor a
  relicensing of this material under Mihraya's Apache 2.0 licence.
  Source text, chapter titles, headings, numbering and narrator fields are
  preserved. Provider status labels are attributed; no named grader is supplied.
  Missing English is not invented: Bukhari 2 records, Tirmidhi 7, Nasa'i 2,
  and all 6293 Mishkat records. Complete Urdu editions are offered for the six
  collections with full Urdu coverage; Tirmidhi's incomplete Urdu is omitted.
  See docs/hadithapi-audit.json and docs/hadithapi-packages.json for source
  counts, exceptions, snapshot/package digests and audit limitations.
  No scholarly textual or grading verification is claimed. The API credential
  is used only in local source-import tooling and is not distributed.

